        "r": 563.6699999999992,
        "b": 720.3039999999999
      },
      "content": "A level switch (7 - View of OSCi), connected to the Elektronikon® regulator of the compressor monitors the condensate level in the second vessel. During normal operation this switch is in the closed position, so that any abnormality (a too high condensate level) opens the electric circuit and triggers the alarm, which is made visible on the Elektronikon® display (see section Warnings).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_745",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4       OSCi (optional)"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_745",
          "title": "General"
        }
      ],
      "page": 71,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0494",
      "reading_order": 753,
      "section": "General",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 91.10949999999997,
        "t": 713.3411000000001,
        "r": 563.6497,
        "b": 661.5640999999999
      },
      "content": "The condensate further flows to the third vessel, through a pipe connecting both lower halves of the vessels. An activated carbon filter (7) cleans the condensate further, and the clean condensate flows out of connection (9). A test outlet (8) is positioned below the normal outlet. Both outlets are connected to the compressor drain plate by their corresponding tubes.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_745",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4       OSCi (optional)"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_745",
          "title": "General"
        }
      ],
      "page": 71,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
